Unreleased
* Whole-vault backup: the note list menu has a new "Back up database" item. It saves a copy of the vault file, encrypted with the same master password. Import the copy to restore it. The backup is checked after it is written.
* Notes with unsaved edits are not in the backup, and the app asks before it goes on.
* New passwords and export passwords are refused when they are common words or follow an obvious pattern (repeated characters, runs such as 1234, keyboard rows). The mixed-kinds rule is removed; length is still at least 12 characters.
* Older copies of a vault are refused instead of opened. A damaged header is reported as damaged, not replaced by an older one.
* The clipboard is cleared only when it still holds the copy the app made.
* Note fields ask the keyboard not to suggest or learn words.
* Plain ZIP and 7z exports ask for confirmation first.
* Leftover plain copies from an interrupted view or export are removed at launch.

2.2 (versionCode 25)
* The olive colour theme is the default now. The unlocked screen has a new header, a search field and filter chips for all items, notes and files.
* The settings rows are grouped into cards under their section titles.
* A read-only entry can no longer be duplicated or copied to the clipboard. It can still be viewed, shared and exported.
* The toolbar of the unlocked screen only shows the settings icon. The sort option and the alphabetical order are removed. Dragging an entry still sets the manual order.
* New launcher icon and in-app logo.
* The About screen has links to check for updates, to the source code and to the issue tracker.
* Fixed a crash when About was opened from the settings.
* Removed the reader for first-release (1.x) files. Open them with 2.0 or 2.1 before updating.
* Removed the option to hide entry names in encrypted exports. Names are kept as they are.
* Encrypted exports are read back and compared with the source data before the file is kept.

2.0 (versionCode 23)
* Security: new vault format (v2). AES-256-GCM replaces AES-128-CBC, so any change to the file is detected. PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 with 600,000 iterations replaces PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA1 with 1,024 iterations.
* Security: databases from 1.x open with the same password and are rewritten in the new format on first open, replacing the old file in place.
* Security: notes are no longer stored as Java serialized objects. Opening an old file only accepts the classes a vault can contain.
* Security: saves are atomic (write to a temporary file, then replace). The old hidden backup copies were removed; they kept copies encrypted with previous passwords.
* Security: the master password is no longer passed between screens in an Intent. The key is kept in memory only while the vault is open and wiped on lock.
* Security: password rules for new and changed passwords: at least 12 characters, mixed kinds unless 16 or longer.
* Security: screenshots and recent-apps previews are blocked. Backups of app data are disabled.
* Security: the app no longer needs storage permission. Databases live in the app's private storage; use Export and Import to move them.
* Security: the vault locks automatically one minute after the app leaves the foreground.
* Fix: editing the only note of a tag while filtered by that tag no longer crashes and no longer loses the edit.
* Fix: tags can be separated by the Chinese comma as well as the English comma.
* Fix: Chinese strings are used for Simplified Chinese locales, including zh-Hans regions. Remaining hard-coded text now comes from resources.
* Fix: the search screen is part of the main list; the separate exported search activity was removed.
* Change: targetSdk 34, minSdk 21, AndroidX libraries, Android Gradle Plugin 8.5.
* Change: the PRNG compatibility patch was removed; the system SecureRandom is used.

